menu "echo_voice"

    config ECHO_VOICE_ENABLED
        bool "Wire the wake word, microphone and Charlie upload"
        default y
        help
            Calls echo_voice_init() from app_main(). It registers the echo_audio
            monitor tap with echo_wakeword, uploads an utterance to echo_ha after
            a detection and plays the server's TTS reply. Requires echo_audio and
            echo_wakeword to be up.

    config ECHO_VOICE_UTTERANCE_MAX_MS
        int "Maximum utterance length (ms)"
        range 1000 30000
        default 8000
        help
            Hard cap on one recording so a stuck session always ends. The turn
            normally closes earlier on silence (ECHO_VOICE_SILENCE_MS).

    config ECHO_VOICE_SILENCE_MS
        int "Trailing silence that ends an utterance (ms)"
        range 300 5000
        default 900
        help
            Once the microphone has been quiet for this long the recording stops
            and "end" is sent, so the server can answer without waiting for the
            full ECHO_VOICE_UTTERANCE_MAX_MS.

    config ECHO_VOICE_SILENCE_RMS
        int "Silence RMS threshold (16-bit full scale)"
        range 1 4000
        default 250
        help
            Frames whose RMS is below this count towards the trailing silence.
            Raise it in a noisy kitchen so the room hum is treated as silence,
            lower it if quiet speech is being cut off.

    config ECHO_VOICE_TTS_RATE_HZ
        int "Server TTS sample rate (Hz)"
        default 22050
        help
            The Charlie server streams 16-bit mono PCM at 22050 Hz. echo_audio
            reconfigures the codec around the reply and restores the capture rate
            afterwards.

endmenu
